### WHEN_SUPPORTED is the default, automatically adding checksums for all modeled httpChecksum operations

Source: https://github.com/aws/aws-sdk-js-v3/blob/main/packages-internal/checksums/src/submodules/flexible-checksums/constants.ts

RequestChecksumCalculation enum and its default. WHEN_SUPPORTED causes checksum headers to be added for all operations with a requestAlgorithmMember (like PutObject), even if requestChecksumRequired is false. WHEN_REQUIRED only adds checksums when requestChecksumRequired is true or the user explicitly sets ChecksumAlgorithm.

```typescript
export const RequestChecksumCalculation = {
  WHEN_SUPPORTED: "WHEN_SUPPORTED",
  WHEN_REQUIRED: "WHEN_REQUIRED",
} as const;

export const DEFAULT_REQUEST_CHECKSUM_CALCULATION = RequestChecksumCalculation.WHEN_SUPPORTED;
```

### Service-specific constructor parameters > S3 > `requestChecksumCalculation` and `responseChecksumValidation`:

Source: https://github.com/aws/aws-sdk-js-v3/blob/main/supplemental-docs/CLIENTS.md

These may be set to `WHEN_REQUIRED` or `WHEN_SUPPORTED`. See https://github.com/aws/aws-sdk-js-v3/issues/6810.
